=== layout: one-panel


@body

- Mendel was the first to count segregants.
- He could not be expected to know all the precautions now needed for completely objective data.
- Rechecking only counts one dislikes can introduce [*systematic bias toward agreement*]{color=#D40000}.
- Even extensive data from other geneticists might not stand up wholly satisfactorily under the &chi;^2^ test.
- The author concludes there was [*no deliberate effort at falsification*]{color=#003FFF}.

@notes

Bullets paraphrase the quotation; the final judgment belongs to its author.

